<section n="1" image-layout="left" id="zewh9bbjfy31f94">
<img query="futuristic office with glowing screens and workers collaborating alongside AI interfaces, warm ambient light" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;futuristic office with glowing screens and workers collaborating alongside AI interfaces, warm ambient light&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;portrait&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;FtRdv&quot;}" class="accent-image">


<div class="body">
<h1>AI &amp; the Labor Market: Is AI Disrupting the Future of Work?</h1>
<p>A clear-eyed look at what the evidence actually says — and what it means for workers, organizations, and policy.</p></div></section>

<section n="2" image-layout="blank" id="ygkne92l2nqq8ge">



<div class="body">
<columns colwidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalalign="center"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/VMSOvYY9Zfap-mZNFpbQI.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom" align="center"></div>
<div verticalalign="center"><h1>The Debate Is Real — and the Stakes Are Enormous</h1>
<smart-layout variant="stats">
<smart-layout-item number="$31T">
<h4>U.S. Economy</h4>
<p>Nearly 60% is labor costs — even a small AI-driven shift moves trillions of dollars.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item number="300M">
<h4>Jobs at Stake</h4>
<p>~27% of OECD positions could be transformed through AI automation globally.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item number="71%">
<h4>Americans Worried</h4>
<p>Concerned AI will permanently put too many people out of work — but the reality is more nuanced.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="3" image-layout="blank" id="a5xvtju18qhvcx1">


<div class="body">
<h1>A Job Is a Bundle of Tasks — Not a Single Thing</h1>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/MfIJj4MZa3u3zYdmzsCic.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<p>AI almost never wipes out whole jobs overnight. It affects <b>tasks first</b> — some get automated, some get supercharged, some create entirely new work.</p>
<aside variant="info">A doctor diagnoses, orders tests, interprets results, and coordinates care. A lawyer drafts, researches, argues, and advises. <b>Each task has a different AI exposure profile.</b></aside>
<p>Understanding this task-level granularity is the key to cutting through the noise in the jobs debate.</p>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="4" image-layout="blank" id="gx1yxs2srsvbzlm">




<div class="body">
<h1>A Three-Layer Framework for Understanding AI's Impact</h1><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/tcJaZfVcfO2bxZF3Nbfe_.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom">
<smart-layout variant="arrows" orientation="horizontal">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Layer 1 — Exposure</h4>
<p>Which tasks can AI plausibly assist or perform today?</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Layer 2 — Adoption</h4>
<p>How quickly will organizations actually deploy AI in practice?</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Layer 3 — Labor Market Response</h4>
<p>What is the net effect on employment, wages, and new job creation?</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout>
<p>These layers constantly feed back into each other — which is why the debate is so contentious.</p></div></section>

<section n="5" image-layout="blank" id="sxkg3gi4f918m3i">





<div class="body">
<h1>Layer 1: Who Is Most Exposed?</h1><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/YUa98dwaWODFnA99ey7mK.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
<smart-layout variant="outlineBoxesWithSideLine" cellsize="10">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>🔴 Highest Exposure</h4>
<p>Text-heavy, information-processing roles: legal research, financial analysis, programming, writing, customer support. High-paying, educated jobs score highest — their work is language and symbol dense.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>🟢 Lowest Exposure</h4>
<p>Embodied, on-site, and interpersonal roles: electricians, roofers, nursing assistants, athletes. Physical manipulation and rich social interaction remain largely AI-resistant today.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="6" image-layout="blank" id="lewtkucy0lguomz">



<div class="body">
<columns colwidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalalign="center"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/0EOfYbjRCdmBrLzAIiyt-.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom" align="center"></div>
<div verticalalign="center"><h1>AI Capabilities Are Racing Ahead of Expectations</h1>
<columns colwidths="[50,50]">
<div>
<h4>Benchmarks Crossed by 2024</h4>
<ul>
<li>Reading comprehension — surpassed human baseline</li>
<li>Visual reasoning — exceeded human performance</li>
<li>PhD-level science questions — at or above human level</li>
<li>Multimodal understanding — achieved in 2024</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div>
<h4>The "New Moore's Law"</h4>
<p>AI's autonomous task capacity doubles every <b>~7 months</b>.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>2026:</b> AI completes a 2-hour task</li>
<li><b>2027:</b> AI completes a full work day (8 hrs)</li>
<li><b>2028:</b> AI completes a full work week (40 hrs)</li>
<li><b>2029:</b> AI completes a full work month (167 hrs)</li>
</ul>
</div>
</columns></div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="7" image-layout="blank" id="vktf2vhfp7va7b6">


<div class="body">
<h1>Layer 2: Exposure ≠ Adoption</h1>
<columns colWidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<p>A job can be highly exposed in theory but untouched in practice. Legal constraints, union rules, data confidentiality, and workflow inertia all slow real-world deployment.</p>
<aside variant="warning">Even technically automatable tasks lag because of cultural and institutional friction — customer backlash, liability concerns, and lack of complementary investments.</aside>
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/36dqHYHpPqMq2xGj1uh38.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
<p>Generative AI hit <b>54.6%</b> overall adult adoption by August 2025 — up 10 points in a single year. Work-specific adoption reached <b>37.4%</b>, still trailing personal use.</p>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="8" image-layout="blank" id="5g1mt4saen6le2i">



<div class="body">
<h1>The Productivity J-Curve: Why Gains Take Time</h1>
<columns colwidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalalign="center"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/q-WW-hRgYtpndVD52_C_A.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom" align="center"></div>
<div verticalalign="center"><smart-layout variant="solidBoxes">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Historical Precedent</h4>
<p>Electricity took decades to raise factory output. PC productivity gains only showed up in U.S. statistics in the mid-1990s — <b>15 years after launch</b>. AI is a general-purpose technology on the same trajectory.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>The Dip Before the Rise</h4>
<p>Early adoption often <b>dips productivity first</b>. 40% of knowledge workers report spending ~2 hours/week fixing low-quality AI outputs — before gains accelerate as workflows mature.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="9" image-layout="blank" id="oxqk47n8oy7h51m">


<div class="body">
<h1>Response 1: Augmentation — AI Makes Workers More Productive</h1>
<smart-layout variant="imagesText" imageposition="top" imageshape="landscape" shapesize="md">
<smart-layout-item>
<img query="knowledge worker at a clean desk using AI software on a laptop, bright modern office, natural daylight" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;knowledge worker at a clean desk using AI software on a laptop, bright modern office, natural daylight&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;landscape&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;9ZXJ3&quot;}">
<h4>Daily AI Users Win</h4>
<p><b>41%</b> of daily AI users rate their productivity "Very Good" vs. <b>26%</b> of non-users. Gains extend to focus, stress management, and job satisfaction.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<img query="radiologist reviewing medical scans on large screens in a darkened hospital reading room" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;radiologist reviewing medical scans on large screens in a darkened hospital reading room&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;landscape&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;4OXha&quot;}">
<h4>The Radiology Lesson</h4>
<p>Geoff Hinton predicted radiologists replaced within 5 years (2016). He was right that AI outperforms on benchmarks — but wrong about demand. Radiology <b>continues to grow</b>, a pattern seen across many exposed professions.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="10" image-layout="blank" id="96nzf3a0hyodrde">


<div class="body">
<h1>Response 2: Displacement — Real, But Concentrated</h1>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/bbGVZndFwjHmGLZpma0Bu.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<p>Clerical and back-office roles face the highest displacement risk: routine document processing, booking, transcription, and standardized communications are repeatedly flagged as highly automatable.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Look for jobs that are repetitive, independent, closed, short, forgiving, and digital — those are the ones most at risk on shorter timescales."</p>
<p><i>— Andrej Karpathy</i></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="11" image-layout="left" id="v8ka2xld8sxoalc">
<img query="diverse team of professionals collaborating in a modern co-working space, new technology tools visible, energetic atmosphere" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;diverse team of professionals collaborating in a modern co-working space, new technology tools visible, energetic atmosphere&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;portrait&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;uv_dl&quot;}" class="accent-image">


<div class="body">
<h1>Response 3: Reinstatement — AI Creates New Roles Too</h1>
<smart-layout variant="iconsText" imagePosition="left" cellSize="xl" orientation="vertical" twoSided="false">
<smart-layout-item>
<icon class="accessory-image" query="history clock" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;icon&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;history clock&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;license&quot;:&quot;All&quot;}},&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;RZAvF&quot;}"></icon>
<h4>History's Pattern</h4>
<p>Technological revolutions rarely destroy jobs in aggregate — they transform them. The PC era created software engineers, IT support, and digital marketers that didn't exist before.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<icon class="accessory-image" query="robot engineer" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;icon&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;robot engineer&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;license&quot;:&quot;All&quot;}},&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;xB_i3&quot;}"></icon>
<h4>New AI Occupations</h4>
<p>AI is already spawning AI engineers, prompt specialists, AI trainers, and trust &amp; safety roles. Productivity gains lower costs, raise demand, and expand existing occupations.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<icon class="accessory-image" query="balance scale fairness" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;icon&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;balance scale fairness&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;license&quot;:&quot;All&quot;}},&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;L1WSd&quot;}"></icon>
<h4>The Real Challenge</h4>
<p>Pace and <b>distribution</b> of change — who adapts fastest and who benefits most — will define AI's true labor market legacy.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="12" image-layout="blank" id="lm7cn9sym50tzdn">





<div class="body">
<h1>What to Watch: Three Questions That Will Determine the Outcome</h1><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/9yfLWL3zkz5f1WStGFzWZ.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
<smart-layout variant="outlineBoxesWithLabel" cellsize="10" numbered="true">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Will adoption accelerate or plateau?</h4>
<p>If AI capability doubles every 4–7 months, the window for workers and institutions to adapt narrows dramatically.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Who captures the productivity gains?</h4>
<p>Higher-wage, higher-educated workers are most exposed — and most positioned to benefit. Lower-wage workers face less disruption but fewer gains.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>How will policy respond?</h4>
<p>Retraining, labor protections, and safety nets will shape whether AI's abundance is broadly shared or concentrated at the top.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="13" image-layout="blank" id="ihs8cfcbq0nfpdw">


